Phase 3: Establish manager creation and publication machinery
  Depends on Phase 2a. Sources: proposal Responsibilities, Initialization and Operation-owned publication; inventory
  manager API, publication and lifecycle contracts. Outcome: one reusable creation/publication boundary.

  ☑ Separate available lookup from native acquire/recover and established-result publication in
    AcquireResource, AcquireWrapperMetadata, ObserveWrapperMetadata, PublishObservedMetadata,
    RefreshMetadata and PublishMetadata. Remove default forced-refresh ambiguity without bypassing
    genuinely unavailable state. Preserve canonical revisions, original association and weak recipients.
  ☑ Move native binding-fact acquisition from GpuVertexAttribBinding constructors/RequireCurrentFacts
    into the GpuResourceManager acquisition/recovery system and its native readers. The helper must not
    call GL.GetVertexArrayIndexed or GL.GetVertexArrayIndexed64 directly. Acquire only requested unknown
    buffer/offset/stride/divisor fields, retain established command results and preserve native-width offsets.
    Use the same manager-owned boundary for registered resources and context-local tools. Preserve original
    owner/context checks, availability, stale-copy detection and non-DSA stale-helper rejection without
    adding a full VAO layout mirror, second registry or canonical metadata writes in the helper.
  ☑ Implement the agreed initialization-record conventions and nullable creation result/handle protocol.
    Canonical structs remain output-only and flag-free; setters track intent automatically. Empty records
    and non-null empty metadata are valid where the resource has no optional inputs/represented facts.
  ☑ Implement manager-owned creation commit, association and typed snapshot delivery, including local tools.
    Failure cleans newly owned native objects/provisional entries, clears the output handle and leaves
    borrowed dependencies intact. Preserve required exceptions, ownership, detach and retirement behavior.
  ☑ Move begin/complete pairing inside explicit command methods where execution is immediate. Capture
    original identity only where needed; simple selectors do not require heap transaction objects.
    Introduce no mandatory per-call closure allocations or generic string/reflection dispatch.
  ☑ Coordinate grouped initialization/updates by original manager entry, not individual wrapper. Suppress
    repeated acquisition and double publication across aliases; publish coherent results only. Interrupted
    groups leave affected facts unavailable while preserving unrelated established facts.
  ☑ Have subagents verify assignment masks, omission/zero/false, conditional defaults, nullable success and
    failure, handoff failure, cleanup, alias groups, reentrancy, context retirement and exactly-once delivery.
    Verify manager-owned vertex-binding acquisition for registered/local resources, field-specific recovery,
    query-free established facts, DSA/fallback behavior, unavailable facts and deletion/name reuse.
  ☑ Completion: the common boundary is verified; family migrations can use it without inventing their
    own acquisition, publication or failure protocols. Existing consumers remain functional during migration.
    GpuVertexAttribBinding contains no native query machinery; its missing facts come through the manager.

  Second source review and independent completion audit passed with no unresolved current-phase findings.
