Phase 4: Migrate buffer and image creation and mutations
  Depends on Phase 3a. Sources: proposal Resource coverage; analysis readers/observers; API B1, T1–T4, R1, I1.
  Each task includes input/default definition, accepted-result publication, failure cleanup and call-site migration.

  ☐ Implement GpuBufferInitialization -> GpuBufferMetadata for GpuBufferObject, GpuVbo, GpuEbo,
    GpuUniformBuffer, GpuShaderStorageBuffer, GpuAtomicCounterBuffer, GpuIndirectBuffer,
    GpuPixelPackBuffer and GpuPixelUnpackBuffer. Keep GpuBufferUploader's role and DSA/fallback dispatch;
    remove RegisterBufferWrapper's duplicate validity reads without treating reserved names as realized.
  ☐ Implement GpuTextureInitialization -> GpuTextureMetadata for GpuTexture, Texture2D, Texture3D,
    DynamicTexture2D, DynamicTexture3D, DynamicTextureCube, DepthTexture, StencilTexture,
    DepthStencilTexture, PmjJitterTexture and CloudBlueNoiseTexture. Preserve constructor inputs,
    allocation choices and GpuLimits use. Derive established mip/face facts as GpuTextureLevelMetadata.
  ☐ Implement GpuRenderbufferInitialization -> GpuRenderbufferMetadata for GpuRenderbuffer.
    Normalize supported sample requests through cached capabilities; use only the proposal's justified
    fallback sample read. Preserve capability-specific storage semantics and avoid repeat allocation.
  ☐ Implement GpuBufferTextureInitialization -> GpuTextureMetadata for GpuBufferView/GpuBufferTexture,
    constructing GpuTextureBufferMetadata centrally. Preserve whole-buffer versus explicit-range semantics,
    native-width ranges, alignment, backing identity and dependency propagation.
  ☐ Implement GpuTextureViewInitialization -> GpuTextureMetadata for GpuTextureView, constructing
    GpuTextureViewMetadata centrally. Preserve source identity/storage revision and view-relative levels.
    Keep renderbuffer-backed texture associations on GpuTextureMetadata/GpuRenderbufferMetadata.
  ☐ Migrate buffer/renderbuffer/texture storage, parameter, mip-generation and association command observers
    to shared execution/publication. Update only affected fields; preserve native acceptance, interruption
    and imported-storage semantics. Base/max changes must not scan unrelated storage; immutable content-only
    mip generation must not invent storage changes. Review ObserveBufferView, TryObserveBufferAssociation,
    ConfigureTextureView and RefreshGeneratedTextureMetadata against this rule.
  ☐ Have subagents verify every migrated family's creation, replacement, failed allocation, defaults,
    output metadata, dependencies and DSA/fallback paths. Compare native queries to the binding-corrected
    baseline; distinguish explicit output exceptions from eliminated descriptor rediscovery.
  ☐ Completion: all listed wrappers use manager creation, no wrapper authors canonical snapshots,
    and narrow image/buffer mutations no longer cause unrelated full reads.

Phase 5: Migrate framebuffer and executable resource creation and publication
  Depends on Phase 4. Sources: proposal coverage/command examples; API F1/P1; analysis corresponding findings.

  ☐ Implement GpuFramebufferInitialization -> GpuFramebufferMetadata for GpuFramebuffer,
    DynamicGpuFramebuffer and StaticGpuFramebuffer. Construct GpuFramebufferImageMetadata centrally;
    keep attachment ownership/static locks, proven multiview semantics and independent routing intact.
  ☐ Refactor RequireNativeAttachment, ObserveFramebufferAttachment, BindFramebufferResource,
    PublishRenderPassMetadata, GpuFramebufferAttachmentDiscovery.Read and ReconcileAttachmentMetadata
    to avoid targeted verification followed by a full scan. Use explicit operation-owned attachment composition and dependency publication.
    GpuFramebufferAttachment receives projected GpuImageMetadata; owned backing uses Phase 4 creation.
    Default framebuffer/surface metadata retains its separate publication path.
  ☐ Implement GpuShaderInitialization -> GpuShaderMetadata for GpuShaderModule: retain established fixed
    stage without rediscovery; compilation/binary loading retains its existing success/lifetime boundary.
  ☐ Implement GpuProgramInitialization -> GpuProgramMetadata for GpuProgramObject/GpuComputePipeline.
    Fresh creation publishes an empty executable without reflection. Preserve GpuProgram/GpuComputeProgram
    composition and existing deferred linking. AcquireCreatedProgramMetadata and AcquireProgramMetadata
    follow separate creation versus discovery contracts.
  ☐ Keep explicit pending identity/context for SubmitProgramLink/CompleteProgramLink behavior. Acquire
    GpuProgramResourceMetadata and GpuProgramTextureUnitMetadata when executable results require it;
    unit/block changes update affected facts without full interface reflection. Preserve unsupported-bindless
    withdrawal, prepared-layout invalidation, full-stage selection and owner-controlled re-preparation.
  ☐ Have subagents verify attachment groups/modes, failed/rejected commands, actual link outcomes,
    deferred retirement/name reuse, unit/block updates, empty programs and unchanged render-pass facts.
  ☐ Completion: framebuffer and executable creation/update paths satisfy canonical publication with
    targeted acquisition and existing ownership, validation and preparation boundaries intact.

Phase 6: Migrate remaining resource creation families
  Depends on Phase 5. Sources: proposal Resource coverage; inventory per-kind schemas and lifecycle.
  Each family uses the Phase 3 protocol, legal inputs only, nullable output and failure cleanup.

  ☐ GpuVao: GpuVertexArrayInitialization -> GpuVertexArrayMetadata; preserve empty revision schema.
  ☐ GpuProgramPipeline: GpuProgramPipelineInitialization -> GpuProgramPipelineMetadata.
  ☐ GpuSampler: GpuSamplerInitialization -> GpuSamplerMetadata; retain authored sampling policy.
  ☐ GpuQuery: GpuQueryInitialization -> GpuQueryMetadata; GpuTimerQuery/GpuTimestampQuery remain composition.
  ☐ GpuFence: GpuSyncInitialization -> GpuSyncMetadata; preserve pointer-width identity and wait semantics.
  ☐ GpuTransformFeedback: GpuTransformFeedbackInitialization -> GpuTransformFeedbackMetadata.
  ☐ GpuSemaphore: GpuSemaphoreInitialization -> GpuSemaphoreMetadata; preserve import ownership.
  ☐ GpuMemoryObject: GpuMemoryObjectInitialization -> GpuMemoryObjectMetadata; preserve import ownership.
  ☐ Keep empty metadata empty; do not add queries or persistent fields to justify initialization records.
    GpuVertexAttribBinding remains a helper with no additional canonical struct.
  ☐ Have subagents verify creation/failure/cleanup and retained metadata/lifetime semantics per family;
    exercise native capability paths where available and explicitly record unexecuted capability cases.
  ☐ Completion: all proposal creation families are migrated and no generic wrapper metadata tracking exists.

Phase 7: Finish external acquisition, recovery and adapter migration
  Depends on Phase 6. Sources: complete analysis method inventory; proposal lookup/acquire/publication;
  inventory association/dependency contracts and API coverage. Outcome: acquisition repairs are ready for audit.

  ☐ Reconcile AcquireExternalImageTexture, AcquireImageMetadata, AcquireBufferTextureBacking,
    AcquireRenderbufferTextureBacking, AssociateImageResource and AssignImageMetadata. Reuse available
    covered entries for raw aliases; keep image projection query-free and retain original backing identity.
  ☐ Migrate BorrowedTexture and external texture/renderbuffer/framebuffer/shader/program wrap/adopt paths
    to lookup or acquisition without creation-time mutation. Unsupported external changes retain explicit
    invalidation/recovery; registry membership alone does not certify observation coverage.
  ☐ Reconcile GpuBufferMetadataReader, GpuTextureMetadataReader, GpuRenderbufferMetadataReader,
    GpuRenderbufferTextureMetadataReader, GpuFramebufferMetadataReader, GpuShaderMetadataReader and
    GpuProgramMetadataReader: preserve unknown-state discovery while narrowing result reads. Avoid repeat
    context-local reads when established results suffice, without trusting stale snapshots after failure.
  ☐ Reconcile every remaining BeginNative*/Complete observer in the analysis with immediate internal
    execution, explicit operation composition or deferred handling. Migrate exact compiler-checked adapters; preserve each allowed
    overload, external dispatch/error behavior, per-object failure and no-content-only metadata work.
